From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:50:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: xpon: en751221: use the stock DBG_DLY settings

The TP-Link stock firmware in O5 on this board reads back
DBG_DLY = 0x001c1440: fine delay 0x14 and the PHY RX delay selector
clear, so the MAC follows the delay the PHY measures. The driver used
fine delay 0x1c and, at overhead programming, forced the selector and
froze half of the RX delay probed at that moment (0x80901c40 in O5).

A frozen RX delay cannot follow the PHY if a downstream glitch moves the
receive phase, which fits the upstream stall seen after a GEM
delineation loss. Use the stock values for EN751221 (lab test).

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c	2026-10-20 19:55:27.575867988 -0300
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c	2026-10-21 08:45:12.608876242 -0300
@@ -610,6 +610,10 @@
 	gpon_rmw(priv, GPON_DBG_DLY, DBG_DLY_FINE_INT_MASK,
 		 FIELD_PREP(DBG_DLY_FINE_INT_MASK,
 			    priv->match_data->gpon_fine_delay));
+	if (!priv->match_data->en7523_gpon_defaults &&
+	    !priv->match_data->gpon_reset_dbg_dly &&
+	    !priv->match_data->gpon_adjust_rx_delay)
+		gpon_clear_bits(priv, GPON_DBG_DLY, DBG_DLY_PHY_RX_DLY_SEL);
 	gpon_rmw(priv, GPON_DBG_IDLE_GEM_THLD, GENMASK(15, 0),
 		 priv->match_data->gpon_idle_gem_threshold);
 
@@ -4765,12 +4769,16 @@
 	.version = econet_en751221,
 	.mode_from_dt = true,
 	.wan_mode_mask = EN751221_SCU_WAN_MODE_MASK,
-	.gpon_fine_delay = 0x1c,
+	/*
+	 * Live register of the TP-Link stock firmware in O5 on this board:
+	 * DBG_DLY = 0x001c1440, i.e. fine delay 0x14 and the PHY RX delay
+	 * left to the hardware (selector clear).
+	 */
+	.gpon_fine_delay = 0x14,
 	.gpon_rsp_time_activation = GPON_RSP_TIME_ACT_EN751221,
 	.gpon_idle_gem_threshold = GPON_IDLE_GEM_THLD_DEFAULT,
 	.gpon_guard_bits_override = GPON_PHY_GUARD_BIT_NUM_EN751221,
 	.gpon_sn_tx_power_mode = GPON_SN_TX_POWER_MODE_LEGACY,
-	.gpon_adjust_rx_delay = true,
 	.mac_irq_via_eth = true,
 	.gpon_rearm_tx_on_overhead = true,
 	.gpon_runtime_tgen = true,
